{"id":622,"slug":"all-that-money-can-buy-a-k-a-the-devil-and-daniel-webster","title":"All That Money Can Buy (a.k.a. The Devil and Daniel Webster)","year":1941,"country":"United States","duration":106,"spine":214,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/622-all-that-money-can-buy-a-k-a-the-devil-and-daniel-webster","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/release_boxshots/5261-6455f02a45615d218398ceaf488250a5/mRuD6vs1cApB7UUpAO3KBn0Bi0j7mr_original.jpg","description":"Jabez Stone is a hardworking farmer trying to make an honest living, but a streak of bad luck tempts him to do the unthinkable: bargain with the devil himself. In exchange for seven years of good fortune, Stone promises “Mr. Scratch” his soul. But when the troubled farmer begins to realize the error of his choice, he enlists the aid of the one man who might save him: the legendary orator and politician Daniel Webster. Directed with stylish flair by William Dieterle, All That Money Can Buy brings the classic short story by Stephen Vincent Benét to life with inspired visuals, an unforgettable, Oscar-winning score by Bernard Herrmann, and a truly diabolical performance from Walter Huston as the devil.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"William Dieterle","slug":"william-dieterle"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Edward Arnold","role":"Daniel Webster","slug":"edward-arnold"},{"actor":"Walter Huston","role":"Mr. Scratch","slug":"walter-huston"},{"actor":"Jane Darwell","role":"Ma Stone","slug":"jane-darwell"},{"actor":"Simone Simon","role":"Belle","slug":"simone-simon"},{"actor":"Gene Lockhart","role":"Squire Slossum","slug":"gene-lockhart"},{"actor":"John Qualen","role":"Miser Stevens","slug":"john-qualen"},{"actor":"Anne Shirley","role":"Mary Stone","slug":"anne-shirley"},{"actor":"James Craig","role":"Jabez Stone","slug":"james-craig"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"William Dieterle","slug":"william-dieterle"},{"role":"Produced by","person":"William Dieterle","slug":"william-dieterle"}